<!DOCTYPE html><html lang=3D"en"><head><meta http-equiv=3D"Content-Type" co=
ntent=3D"text/html; charset=3DUTF-8"><link rel=3D"stylesheet" type=3D"text/=
css" href=3D"cid:css-16901580-8fdc-42e7-8fe8-711447d7905e@mhtml.blink" />

<meta name=3D"viewport" content=3D"width=3Ddevice-width, initial-scale=3D1"=
>
<title>Canonical AST Transformer</title>

</head>
<body>

<h1>Canonical AST Transformer</h1>
<p class=3D"sub">
  Enter an arithmetic expression (<code>+ =E2=88=92 * ( )</code>). Three vi=
ews of the value:
  <b>Canonical</b> factors it into a tree rooted at <code>*</code> with eve=
ry prime leg drawn in its
  <code>6k=C2=B11</code> skeleton (<code>5 =3D 2=C2=B73=E2=88=921</code>, <=
code>7 =3D 2=C2=B73+1</code>, =E2=80=A6) =E2=80=94
  so every <b>composite</b> gets a <code>*</code> root, while a <b>prime</b=
> has no factor and stays at a
  <code>=C2=B11</code> remainder; <b>Expand</b> applies the distributive la=
w down to atoms;
  <b>6k=C2=B11 core</b> peels the value into sixes plus its remainder.
</p>

<div class=3D"controls">
  <input id=3D"exprInput" placeholder=3D"e.g.  2*2*2*3+1   or   3*(2*3-1)">
  <button>Canonical (root =C3=97)</button>
  <button class=3D"ghost">Clear</button>
</div>

<div class=3D"toolbar">
  <span class=3D"label">Distributive:</span>
  <button class=3D"alt">Expand one level</button>
  <button class=3D"alt">Expand fully</button>
  <button class=3D"alt2">Show 6k=C2=B11 core</button>
  <span id=3D"levelTag" class=3D"label"></span>
</div>

<div class=3D"examples">
  Try:
  <a>35</a>
  <a>49</a>
  <a>143</a>
  <a>97</a>
  <a>2*2*2*3+1</a>
</div>

<div id=3D"status"></div>

<div class=3D"panels">
  <div class=3D"card">
    <h2 id=3D"treeTitle">Tree</h2>
    <div id=3D"treeArea" class=3D"tree-container"></div>
  </div>
  <div>
    <div class=3D"card" style=3D"margin-bottom:16px">
      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <div id=3D"summary" class=3D"kv">=E2=80=94</div>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"card">
      <h2 id=3D"stepsTitle">Detail</h2>
      <ol id=3D"steps" class=3D"steps"><li>=E2=80=94</li></ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>





</body></html>
